@@ -101,31 +101,40 @@ ### Issue a ticket
 ### Call the next ticket
 
 ```text
-Attendant
+Attendant (trusted caller; authorization is a later layer)
    |
    v
-Authorized call action
+App\Actions\CallNextTicket(queue, user, CallMode)
    |
    v
-Load waiting state for the queue
+BEGIN; lock the queue row; re-read is_active (reject inactive queue)
    |
    v
-Apply deterministic priority + age + fairness rules
+Pick the first waiting ticket of the queue for the mode:
+priority DESC, issued_at ASC, id ASC (+ fairness in `any` mode)
    |
    v
-Atomically mark exactly one ticket as called
+Lock the candidate row; still waiting? no -> skip it, pick the next
    |
    v
-Return called ticket / display payload
+Set status = called, called_at = now(), called_by_user_id; COMMIT
+   |
+   v
+Return the updated ticket (NoWaitingTicketsException if none eligible)
 ```
 
-The implementation must prevent two concurrent attendants from successfully
-calling the same waiting ticket. The exact locking strategy belongs to the
-implementation and database transaction layer; the domain invariant is that a
-ticket can be called only once.
-
-> TODO (follow-up from review): link the test covering the single-call
-> invariant and concurrent-call protection once implemented.
+`App\Actions\CallNextTicket` takes `App\Enums\CallMode` (`any`,
+`priority_only`, `normal_only`). The queue row lock serializes concurrent
+`CallNextTicket` calls and deactivation; `Ticket::call()` does not lock the
+queue, so the candidate row is locked and its `waiting` status re-checked
+before marking it called. A ticket can therefore be called only once.
+`lockForUpdate()` is a no-op on SQLite (tests); the re-check still runs.
+Fairness is evaluated from the called-ticket history of the queue (see
+[`business-rules.md`](business-rules.md#ordering-and-fairness)).
+
+Covered by `tests/Feature/CallNextTicketTest.php` (ordering, modes, fairness,
+inactive/stale queue, exactly-once skip when a candidate is called
+concurrently).
 
 ## Authorization boundary
 
